==Portuguese==

===Etymology===
{{rfe|lang=pt}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Pt tomar.ogg|Audio}}

===Verb===
{{pt-verb}}

# {{transitive|lang=pt}} to [[take]] (something);
#: "''Fui ao banco '''tomar''' meu dinheiro.''" - I went to the bank to take my money.
# {{transitive|lang=pt}} to [[steal]] (something);
#: "''O ladrão '''tomou''' todo o meu dinheiro.''" - The thief has stolen all my money.
# {{transitive|lang=pt}} to consider that something or someone (direct object) is other thing or other one (''[[por]]'');
#: "''Eu '''tomei''' a Maria por corrupta.''" - I thought Mary was corrupt.
# {{transitive|lang=pt}} to [[drink]];
#: "''Eu '''tomei''' suco.''" - I drank juice.
# {{intransitive|lang=pt}} to [[consume]] [[alcoholic]] [[beverage]]s;
#: "''Ele '''toma''' muito, durante os finais de semana.''" - He drinks a lot, on weekends.

====Conjugation====
{{pt-conj|tom|ar}}

====See also====
* [[beber]]

